# TycStation Lightshow is configured in the app, not the environment.
#
# Everything — outputs, MIDI, the live input and its Python, the bind
# address, port and access token — is set in its Rig, Sources and Settings
# views (http://localhost:3000/#settings) and stored in
# config/settings.json (mode 0600, gitignored). Anything not set uses the
# built-in default, so there is nothing to copy or fill in here to get started.
#
# A .env in the directory the server is started from is still read (by Node's
# own loader; a variable already set in the environment wins). What it can
# usefully hold:
#
#DEBUG_MIDI=1                    # log every incoming MIDI message
#LIGHTSHOW_DATA_DIR=/srv/show    # config/, logs/ and the .venv the live input tries first
#LIGHTSHOW_CONFIG_DIR=/srv/show  # where settings, the show, cues and the MIDI map live
#LIGHTSHOW_LOG_DIR=/var/log/show # where lightshow.log is written (default: logs/)
#LOG_LEVEL=debug                 # trace, debug, info (the default), warn, error
#LOG_FORMAT=json                 # pretty or json in the terminal (default: pretty on a terminal, else json)
#LIGHTSHOW_SUPERVISOR=0          # run the server without the supervisor npm start puts it under
